<title>AUSTRALIA: C-C Amatil half year net A$58.1 mln.</title>
<headline>C-C Amatil half year net A$58.1 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net				     58.1  vs 57.8</p>
<p>    Interim dividend (cents)	   9.5  vs  9.5</p>
<p>NOTE: Coca-Cola Amatil Ltd is a soft drink maker and is 33 percent owned by The Coca-Cola Co. The company said net profit including Philippines operations was A$98.1 million. Analysts had expected a first half pre-abnormals net profit of about A$60 million not including Philippines operations. C-C Amatil merged with San Miguel Corp's bottling unit in July.  </p>
<p>    Operating profit		    146.9  vs 93.3</p>
<p>    Sales (billion)			 1.87 vs  1.79</p>
<p>    Other income			   83.9  vs 39.5</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			    14.2  vs 11.7</p>
<p>    Abnormal items			 nil   vs nil</p>
<p>Dividend is unfranked</p>
<p>Pay date Sept 30</p>
<p>Reg date Sept 12</p>
<p>    Tax					48.2 vs 31.2</p>
<p>    Interest				107.4 vs 75.5</p>
<p>    Depreciation			  127.5 vs 88.4</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
